Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Interactive continuous ray tracing on the local parabolic mirror section\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.983962847433036*^9, 
  3.983962852237754*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c524e142-ea92-455d-ba16-\
d8780dd8af51"],

Cell["\<\
This interactive visualization shows,in the local x\[Dash]z plane:
\t-the local parabolic mirror section,
\t-the corresponding geometric focus,
\t-the parabola vertex,
\t-the local optical axis,
\t-a bundle of parallel incident rays,
\t-and the reflected rays directed toward the focus.

Physical interpretation:
\tThe incident radiation is modeled as a plane wave,i.e.,as a family of \
parallel rays arriving from the concave side of the reflector.

The direction of these incident rays is defined by the local optical axis of \
the parabola,given by the line joining:
\t-the geometric focus,
\t-and the vertex of the parabolic section.

Then, from each point of incidence on the mirror,a reflected ray is drawn \
toward the geometric focus,reproducing the ideal optical property of a \
parabola.

Additionally,a fixed red circle is superimposed,representing the \
cross-section of the distributed reactor.\
\>", "Text",
