Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Continuous 3 D ray tracing on the parametric mirror surface", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9839629412094193`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"41719333-32fc-4583-82e8-\
f52956aa1bdc"],

Cell["\<\
This block builds an interactive 3D ray-tracing visualization on the mirror \
surface for day 170. 

Geometric convention:
\t-z is the vertical coordinate.
\t-The mirror opens toward the region x<0.
\t-Therefore,incident solar radiation must arrive from x<0 toward the concave \
reflective surface.

Optical convention:
\t-All incident rays form a plane wave.
\t-Therefore,all incident rays are parallel.
\t-For each TST, they share the same elevation and azimuth.
\t-Only illuminated points on the concave surface are considered.
\t-Reflected directions are computed using the law of reflection.
\t-Only reflected rays intersecting the cylindrical reactor are retained.

Requirements:
\t-GenerateSurfaceAndFocus[dn] already defined.
\t-day170=GenerateSurfaceAndFocus[170] already computed.
\t-SurfacesDay170 and ReactorDay170 available.
\t-h[dn,TST] and azimuth[dn,TST] defined.*)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.983962972691882*^9, 
  3.983963003589871*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"97e21b94-c451-418f-b2cf-\
d6cea0e1726a"],

