Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Continuous power - density distribution on the reactor skin", \
"Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.983968943958733*^9},ExpressionUUID->"c7aec374-d5ff-4ce2-a610-\
8bd4a79ae7ae"],

Cell["\<\
This block computes and visualizes the power-density distribution over the \
lateral surface of the reactor,unwrapped into 2D.

Final map coordinates:
\t-Horizontal axis:position along the reactor[m],from 0 to approximately 30 \
m.
\t-Vertical axis:perimeter coordinate on the reactor skin[m],from 0 to 2 Pi R.

Represented quantity:
\t-Power density on the reactor skin[W/m^2].

Important visual remark:
\tThe upper color limit is fixed using a percentile in order to avoid color \
saturation and better reveal local variations.*)

ASSUMED AVAILABLE FROM PREVIOUS BLOCKS

This block assumes that the following quantities are already defined or \
computed:
\t-dn
\t-surfaceGrid=SurfacesDay170
\t-reactorCenterline=Flatten[ReactorDay170,1]
\t-nCurves,nPts
\t-reactorRadius
\t-nearestReactorPoint
\t-normalAt[i,j]
\t-illuminatedQ[i,j,TST]
\t-reflectedDirAt[i,j,TST]
\t-h[dn,TST],azimuth[dn,TST] 

If needed,the following lines could be uncommented and adapted:
\tdn=170;
\tsurfaceGrid=SurfacesDay170;
\treactorCenterline=Flatten[ReactorDay170,1];
\tnCurves=Length[surfaceGrid];
\tnPts=Length[surfaceGrid[[1]]];
\treactorRadius=0.65/2;
\tnearestReactorPoint=Nearest[reactorCenterline\[Rule]\"Index\"];*)\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9839690774484987`*^9, 
  3.983969125300199*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6ad01641-736d-4614-a11e-\
cd47c711cc20"],

