Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Thermal model on the reactor skin using finite-differences", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9839691648892393`*^9, 
  3.983969178075428*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c595f2df-3685-4186-a47f-\
c1a746a08d8d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
This block computes the steady - state temperature field on the reactor skin \
from the optical power - density distribution q (s, u) .\
\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.983969208201035*^9, 
  3.9839692104323597`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b6b7865f-15fa-4050-b720-\
5b9aaa4a7b88"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "\n        Physical effects included :\n \t-thermal conduction along the \
steel wall,\n\t-convection with ambient air, -thermal radiation to the \
surroundings .\n   \n   Coordinates used :\n           -s : longitudinal \
coordinate along the reactor[m]\n           -u : perimeter coordinate on the \
reactor skin[m] \n \n Boundary conditions :\n\t-periodic in u (because the \
reactor is cylindrical),\n\t-zero flux at s = 0 and s = L (homogeneous \
Neumann condition) .\n      \nSolved equation :\nrho cp e dT/dt = ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["k", "e"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "cf392716-cef4-4685-b51e-683e1c5d88d5"],
 " Laplacian (T) + q - h (T - Tamb) - eps sigma (T^4 - Tamb^4) \n\n where :\n \
 \t-rho cp e dT/dt represents the surface thermal inertia,\n\t -",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["k", "e"], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "d241ab22-fd02-43c5-8ed5-dd0a8081f38a"],
 " Laplacian (T) represents thermal diffusion in the wall,\n\t -q is the \
incident heat flux,\n\t -h (T - Tamb) are convective losses,\n\t -eps sigma \
(T^4 - Tamb^4) are radiative losses .\n   \n   Numerical strategy :\n         \
    The stationary problem is not solved directly; instead, the system is \
integrated in pseudo - time until convergence is reached . At steady state, \
dT/dt -> 0.*)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.983969197058015*^9, 
  3.983969388717265*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1bafd05a-d186-468e-b190-\
0365ef1dab02"],

